k","mombasa"],"summary":"It is possible to visit the mangrove forests of the Kombeni and Tsalu rivers which form the Tudor Creek. To do that, ask a fisherman at Cape Kiberamni or Junda Creek to take you there.","summarySource":"wikivoyage","wikivoyageTitle":"Mombasa"},{"id":"mombasa_wv_nguuni_sanctury","areaId":"mombasa","name":"Nguuni Sanctury","category":"landmark","tags":["photo"],"location":{"lat":-3.9849,"lng":39.696},"visitMinutes":60,"priceLevel":1,"photoSeed":"mombasa_wv_nguuni_sanctury","tickets":[{"vendor":"Official","url":"http://lifeinmombasa.com/nguuni-nature-sanctuary/","official":true}],"signals":{"commonsNearby":0,"wikidataSitelinks":0,"fetchedAt":"2026-10-21"},"hashtags":["nguunisanctury","mombasa"],"summary":"The Nguuni Nature sanctuary is 4 km from Lafarge Bamburi Cement on the Nguu Tatu Hills and is the home to many animal, like giraffes, elands, oryx, waterbucks, ostriches and many different birds. It is a very good place to experience nature and safari feeling on foot. The wetlands with small lakes are an interesting place for bird watchers, who have the opportunity to observe many different specie","summarySource":"wikivoyage","wikivoyageTitle":"Mombasa"},{"id":"mombasa_wv_krapf_memorial","areaId":"mombasa","name":"Krapf Memorial","category":"landmark","tags":["photo"],"location":{"lat":-4.05581,"lng":39.68301},"visitMinutes":60,"priceLevel":1,"photoSeed":"mombasa_wv_krapf_memorial","tickets":[],"signals":{"commonsNearby":0,"wikidataSitelinks":0,"fetchedAt":"2026-10-21"},"hashtags":["krapfmemorial","mombasa"],"summary":"This 19th-century monument memorialises the German explorer and missionary Johann Ludwig Krapf who became the first European to see Mount Kenya with the help of the Kamba people.","summarySource":"wikivoyage","wikivoyageTitle":"Mombasa"},{"id":"mombasa_mbaraki_pillar","areaId":"mombasa","name":"Mbaraki Pillar","category":"landmark","tags":["views","photo"],"location":{"lat":-4.07314,"lng":39.66446},"visitMinutes":60,"priceLevel":2,"photoSeed":"mombasa_mbaraki_pillar","tickets":[],"signals":{"commonsDepicts":0,"commonsNearby":0,"wikidataSitelinks":0,"fetchedAt":"2026-10-21"},"hashtags":["mbarakipillar","mombasa"],"hours":{"week":[{"open":"10:00","close":"19:00"},{"open":"10:00","close":"19:00"},{"open":"10:00","close":"19:00"},{"open":"10:00","close":"19:00"},{"open":"10:00","close":"19:00"},{"open":"10:00","close":"19:00"},{"open":"10:00","close":"19:00"}],"note":"Typical hours — check the official site"},"bestLight":"sunset","summary":"The Mbaraki Pillar is a historic tower monument made of coral stone, approximately 14 metres high. It is considered the second-oldest historic monument in Mombasa after Fort Jesus and is a listed national monument. The hollow tower is also known locally as Mnarani (‘place of the tower’). Whilst an adjacent mosque dates back to the 15th century (c. 1400–1450), the construction of the tower itself i","summarySource":"wikivoyage","wikivoyageTitle":"Mombasa"},{"id":"mombasa_wv_commonwealth_war_cemetery_mbaraki","areaId":"mombasa","name":"Commonwealth War Cemetery Mbaraki","category":"landmark","tags":["photo"],"location":{"lat":-4.06735,"lng":39.66549},"visitMinutes":60,"priceLevel":1,"photoSeed":"mombasa_wv_commonwealth_war_cemetery_mbaraki","tickets":[{"vendor":"Official","url":"http://www.cwgc.org/find-a-cemetery/cemetery/12204/MOMBASA%20%28MBARAKI%29%20CEMETERY","official":true}],"signals":{"commonsNearby":0,"wikidataSitelinks":0,"fetchedAt":"2026-10-21"},"hashtags":["commonwealthwarcemeterymbaraki","mombasa"],"hours":{"week":[{"open":"06:00","close":"18:00"},{"open":"06:00","close":"18:00"},{"open":"06:00","close":"18:00"},{"open":"06:00","close":"18:00"},{"open":"06:00","close":"18:00"},{"open":"06:00","close":"18:00"},{"open":"06:00","close":"18:00"}]},"summary":"The final resting place for 197 Commonwealth soldiers of which 51 died in World War I and 146 in World War II, plus two French soldiers.","summarySource":"wikivoyage","wikivoyageTitle":"Mombasa"},{"id":"mombasa_wv_commonwealth_war_cemetery_manyimbo","areaId":"mombasa","name":"Commonwealth War Cemetery Manyimbo","category":"landmark","tags":["photo"],"location":{"lat":-4.03952,"lng":39.66523},"visitMinutes":60,"priceLevel":1,"photoSeed":"mombasa_wv_commonwealth_war_cemetery_manyimbo","tickets":[{"vendor":"Official","url":"http://www.cwgc.org/find-a-cemetery/cemetery/2019409/MOMBASA%20%28MANYIMBO%29%20WAR%20CEMETERY","official":true}],"signals":{"commonsNearby":0,"wikidataSitelinks":0,"fetchedAt":"2026-10-21"},"hashtags":["commonwealthwarcemeterymanyimbo","mombasa"],"hours":{"week":[{"open":"06:00","close":"18:00"},{"open":"06:00","close":"18:00"},{"open":"06:00","close":"18:00"},{"open":"06:00","close":"18:00"},{"open":"06:00","close":"18:00"},{"open":"06:00","close":"18:00"},{"open":"06:00","close":"18:00"}]},"summary":"Graves of 225 Commonwealth soldiers and two other soldiers from World War II.","summarySource":"wikivoyage","wikivoyageTitle":"Mombasa"},{"id":"mombasa_wv_wild_waters_amusement_park","areaId":"mombasa","name":"Wild Waters Amusement Park","category":"park","tags":["nature","photo"],"location":{"lat":-4.03957,"lng":39.70444},"visitMinutes":60,"priceLevel":0,"photoSeed":"mombasa_wv_wild_waters_amusement_park","tickets":[{"vendor":"Official","url":"https://www.facebook.com/WildWatersKenya","official":true}],"signals":{"commonsNearby":0,"wikidataSitelinks":0,"fetchedAt":"2026-10-21"},"hashtags":["wildwatersamusementpark","mombasa"],"hours":{"week":[{"open":"10:00","close":"18:00"},{"open":"10:00","close":"18:00"},{"open":"10:00","close":"18:00"},{"open":"10:00","close":"18:00"},{"open":"10:00","close":"18:00"},{"open":"10:00","close":"18:00"},{"open":"10:00","close":"18:00"}]},"bestLight":"golden","summary":"Water amusement park with 15 different toboggans. On hot days this is a good place to cool yourself. The water park is reportedly modern and clean. Other activities on site include a gaming arcade, a \"disco arena\" and several theme rides as well as food court.","summarySource":"wikivoyage","wikivoyageTitle":"Mombasa"},{"id":"mombasa_mombasa_marine_national_park_and_marine_reserve","areaId":"mombasa","name":"Mombasa Marine National Park and Marine Reserve","category":"park","tags":["nature","photo"],"location":{"lat":-4.049,"lng":39.72366},"visitMinutes":60,"priceLevel":0,"photoSeed":"mombasa_mombasa_marine_national_park_and_marine_reserve","tickets":[{"vendor":"Official","url":"http://kws.go.ke/content/mombasa-marine-national-park-reserve","official":true}],"signals":{"commonsDepicts":0,"commonsNearby":0,"wikidataSitelinks":0,"fetchedAt":"2026-10-21"},"hashtags":["mombasamarinenationalparkandmarinereserve","mombasa"],"bestLight":"golden","summary":"For divers the main attraction is the Leven coral reef in the Mombasa Marine National Park and Marine Reserve. Including reef crest habitats of the Bamburi-Nyali fringing reef and a part of the lagoon, this is the Kenya's most popular marine park. It has an area of 10 km2 and is part of a larger reserve of 200 km2. There are three wrecks that can be visited.","summarySource":"wikivoyage","wikivoyageTitle":"Mombasa","names":{"de":"Mombasa Marine Nationalpark und Reservat","fr":"Parc national maritime et réserve marine de Mombasa","it":"Parco nazionale marino e riserva di Mombasa"},"photo":{"url":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c5/Wooden_boat_off-shore_in_Mombasa%27s_Marine_Park.jpg/1280px-Wooden_boat_off-shore_in_Mombasa%27s_Marine_Park.jpg","thumb":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c5/Wooden_boat_off-shore_in_Mombasa%27s_Marine_Park.jpg/500px-Wooden_boat_off-shore_in_Mombasa%27s_Marine_Park.jpg","w":1200,"h":800,"author":"McKay Savage from London, UK","license":"CC BY 2.0","licenseUrl":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/2.0","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Wooden_boat_off-shore_in_Mombasa%27s_Marine_Park.jpg"}},{"id":"mombasa_wv_kongowea_market","areaId":"mombasa","name":"Kongowea Market","category":"food","tags":["food","markets"],"location":{"lat":-4.04017,"lng":39.68275},"visitMinutes":75,"priceLevel":1,"photoSeed":"mombasa_wv_kongowea_market","tickets":[],"signals":{},"hashtags":["kongoweamarket","mombasa"],"hours":{"week":[{"open":"03:00","close":"13:00"},{"open":"03:00","close":"13:00"},{"open":"03:00","close":"13:00"},{"open":"03:00","close":"13:00"},{"open":"03:00","close":"13:00"},{"open":"03:00","close":"13:00"},{"open":"03:00","close":"13:00"}]},"summary":"Kongowea market is one of the largest in Kenya with over 1500 stalls and an area of 4.75 ha. Worth visiting for its ambiance, colors and smells. Take care with meat products because they are not always what the signs say. If you want to take photos of the vendors and their stalls, ask permission first. Also, pickpockets operate in the market, so don't show your expensive camera or phone more than ","summarySource":"wikivoyage","wikivoyageTitle":"en:Mombasa"},{"id":"mombasa_wv_bob_s_bar","areaId":"mombasa","name":"Bob's Bar","category":"nightlife","tags":["nightlife"],"location":{"lat":-4.02104,"lng":39.71912},"visitMinutes":90,"photoSeed":"mombasa_wv_bob_s_bar","tickets":[],"signals":{},"hashtags":["bobsbar","mombasa"],"hours":{"week":[{"open":"18:00","close":"23:59"},{"open":"18:00","close":"23:59"},{"open":"18:00","close":"23:59"},{"open":"18:00","close":"23:59"},{"open":"18:00","close":"23:59"},{"open":"18:00","close":"23:59"},{"open":"18:00","close":"23:59"}],"note":"Typical hours — check the official site"},"bestLight":"night","summary":"Lively and popular bar near Tembo. This bar and grill is where a lot of great nights out get started. One of the few bars that is open until sunrise! 3 bars, one of them has a terrace. Disco. Serves food.","summarySource":"wikivoyage","wikivoyageTitle":"en:Mombasa"},{"id":"mombasa_wv_tamarind_mombasa","areaId":"mombasa","name":"Tamarind Mombasa","category":"food","tags":["food"],"location":{"lat":-4.04942,"lng":39.6814},"visitMinutes":75,"priceLevel"